# ARK Constitution

**Full document:** [ark-constitution-v1.md](../../docs/ecosystem/ark-constitution-v1.md)

This constrains future decisions. Not a roadmap. Not architecture. A constitution.

## Constitutional principle

**Coherence over capability.**

When adding capability conflicts with internal consistency, coherence wins.

## Hierarchy of evidence (strongest first)

1. Operational truth (Authority)
2. Observed behavior (Notebook)
3. Repeated sentences (Evolution)
4. Instrumentation (Confirmation)
5. Opinion

Opinion needs grounding above before it reshapes the product.

## Before building

Ask **"What has earned the right to exist?"** — not *"What's next?"*

First answer to most new ideas: **"Not yet."**

No repeated sentence → notebook, not `main`. See [ark-earned-intelligence.mdc](ark-earned-intelligence.mdc).

## Guardrail, not gate

Constitution constrains **implementation**, not **observation**. Everything may be observed; almost nothing ships without evidence. Notebook is the safest place in ARK. Vision outranks evidence at **architecture** only — workflow is earned after.

## Significant PRs

Answer **litmus (five)** + **four grammars**: Authority · Projection · Workspace · Evolution. See [ark-pr-doctrine-review.mdc](ark-pr-doctrine-review.mdc).

## Product purpose

Reduce hesitation. Preserve momentum. Operational truth explainable at every step. When goals conflict, **coherence over capability**.

## Truth stack

```
Events are truth.
Projections summarize truth.
Narratives explain truth.
Evidence justifies truth.
```

Full doctrine: [ark-truth-stack-v1.md](../../docs/ecosystem/ark-truth-stack-v1.md) · [ark-projection-rule.mdc](ark-projection-rule.mdc) · [ark-explainability-doctrine.mdc](ark-explainability-doctrine.mdc)

**Explainability Rule:** If evidence cannot be shown, do not present the claim as operational truth.

**Earned Authority:** If operational truth cannot be traced, do not publish the claim outside the shop. See [ark-earned-authority.mdc](ark-earned-authority.mdc).
